From: Bohrium332 <ruiqian.tang@seeed.cc>
Subject: [PATCH] overlays: rpi: reComputer-R22: drive RS485_POWER_EN high

The reComputer-R22 overlay declares RS485_POWER_EN (pca9535_1 pin 11)
in hog style but omits the "gpio-hog;" property, so the node is inert
and the pin floats at boot. reComputer-R2x-base hogs the same rail
enable output-high.

The net is bridged by R244 to ISO_PWR_EN, the enable of the isolated
5V rail (U36) that powers the field side of the isolated RS-232
(SP3232EEA) and both isolated RS-485 (ISO3082DW) transceivers. Board
bring-up shows the rail currently comes up with the pin floating, but
leaving an undefined level on a supply-enable input is fragile; drive
it high at boot for a defined state and R2x parity.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Seeed-specific hardware bring-up]
---
diff --git a/overlays/rpi/reComputer-R22-overlay.dts b/overlays/rpi/reComputer-R22-overlay.dts
index 8b04422..be9f55a 100644
--- a/overlays/rpi/reComputer-R22-overlay.dts
+++ b/overlays/rpi/reComputer-R22-overlay.dts
@@ -167,8 +167,9 @@
 				};
 				
 				RS485_POWER_EN {
+					gpio-hog;
 					gpios = <&pca9535_1 11 0>;
-					output-low;
+					output-high;
 					line-name = "RS485_POWER_EN";
 				};
